1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,615
Kewalram Chanrai Group.

2
00:00:02,745 --> 00:00:05,257
EJO 100, Enterprise
Platform.

3
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:06,805
Built by JusTech.

4
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,654
This is EJO 100: one
platform for the whole

5
00:00:11,784 --> 00:00:12,022
group,

6
00:00:12,152 --> 00:00:14,289
from the front desk to the
boardroom.

7
00:00:14,419 --> 00:00:17,597
Every member of staff signs
in with their own account,

8
00:00:17,727 --> 00:00:19,863
and sees only what their
role allows.

9
00:00:19,993 --> 00:00:23,049
Let's start where the day
starts, at the front desk.

10
00:00:24,679 --> 00:00:26,839
The dashboard is the morning
briefing.

11
00:00:26,969 --> 00:00:29,492
Live counts of the vehicles
in the workshop,

12
00:00:29,622 --> 00:00:32,686
jobs waiting on approval,
parts that need reordering,

13
00:00:32,816 --> 00:00:35,338
and everything that changed
since yesterday.

14
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:37,749
While a page loads, the EJO
mark pulses,

15
00:00:37,879 --> 00:00:40,703
so you always know the
system is working for you.

16
00:00:43,412 --> 00:00:45,098
Customers live in one place.

17
00:00:45,228 --> 00:00:48,016
A profile holds the
vehicles, every job card,

18
00:00:48,146 --> 00:00:51,647
every payment, and the full
history of the relationship.

19
00:00:51,777 --> 00:00:53,138
Nothing is typed twice,

20
00:00:53,268 --> 00:00:56,510
and nothing is lost when a
member of staff moves on.

21
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:00,185
The workshop runs on job
cards.

22
00:01:00,315 --> 00:01:04,043
A job card follows a vehicle
from gate to gate: intake,

23
00:01:04,173 --> 00:01:07,409
inspection, estimate, parts,
work done, billing,

24
00:01:07,539 --> 00:01:08,251
and release.

25
00:01:08,381 --> 00:01:10,987
Every step records who did
it and when,

26
00:01:11,117 --> 00:01:14,845
so a supervisor can see the
state of the whole floor at

27
00:01:14,975 --> 00:01:15,476
a glance.

28
00:01:17,106 --> 00:01:20,073
Every document prints on the
group's own letterhead.

29
00:01:20,203 --> 00:01:22,098
The logo sits beside the
wordmark,

30
00:01:22,228 --> 00:01:25,017
the green rule carries the
group name beneath it,

31
00:01:25,147 --> 00:01:27,638
and the executing branch
follows underneath,

32
00:01:27,768 --> 00:01:30,735
exactly as on the printed
job card the workshop uses

33
00:01:30,865 --> 00:01:31,093
today.

34
00:01:32,839 --> 00:01:35,066
Inventory knows every part
on the shelf:

35
00:01:35,196 --> 00:01:38,247
what is in stock, what is
reserved against a job card,

36
00:01:38,377 --> 00:01:40,662
what has just arrived on a
goods receipt,

37
00:01:40,792 --> 00:01:43,255
and what has fallen below
its reorder level.

38
00:01:43,385 --> 00:01:46,259
The store manager sees the
numbers before the shelf

39
00:01:46,389 --> 00:01:46,907
runs empty.

40
00:01:48,537 --> 00:01:51,246
Approvals route themselves
to the right person.

41
00:01:51,376 --> 00:01:52,937
A supervisor approves first,

42
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:54,930
the manager gives the final
word,

43
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,950
and the rules make sure
nobody signs off their own

44
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:58,433
request.

45
00:01:58,563 --> 00:01:59,943
Each decision is one tap,

46
00:02:00,073 --> 00:02:02,842
and the requester is told
the moment it happens.

47
00:02:04,472 --> 00:02:06,831
At the gate, security
registers visitors,

48
00:02:06,961 --> 00:02:09,440
logs every vehicle coming in
and going out,

49
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:12,717
and issues exit passes and
road test passes that print

50
00:02:12,847 --> 00:02:14,963
with a reference the gate
can verify.

51
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:18,179
Who is on the premises right
now is always one screen

52
00:02:18,309 --> 00:02:18,482
away.

53
00:02:22,139 --> 00:02:24,071
The schedule brings
meetings, rooms,

54
00:02:24,201 --> 00:02:26,991
visitors and appointments
into one calendar for the

55
00:02:27,121 --> 00:02:27,736
whole branch.

56
00:02:27,866 --> 00:02:29,511
Book a room, invite
colleagues,

57
00:02:29,641 --> 00:02:31,401
and the gate knows who to
expect.

58
00:02:33,031 --> 00:02:35,255
Customer care runs the
support centre.

59
00:02:35,385 --> 00:02:38,044
Every request becomes a
ticket with an owner,

60
00:02:38,174 --> 00:02:39,779
a deadline, and a follow-up.

61
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:42,753
Service hours and teams are
set by the business,

62
00:02:42,883 --> 00:02:43,992
not by the software.

63
00:02:45,622 --> 00:02:48,382
Enyo is the assistant built
into the platform.

64
00:02:48,512 --> 00:02:51,901
Ask it in plain language and
it answers from the group's

65
00:02:52,031 --> 00:02:52,655
own records,

66
00:02:52,785 --> 00:02:55,608
with the same permissions as
the person asking.

67
00:02:55,738 --> 00:02:57,870
It summarises, drafts, and
explains,

68
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,195
and it never sees data it
should not.

69
00:03:01,825 --> 00:03:05,236
Leadership sees across every
branch: workflow analytics,

70
00:03:05,366 --> 00:03:07,766
headquarters dashboards, and
a complete,

71
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,157
append-only audit log.

72
00:03:09,287 --> 00:03:12,446
Every action in the system
can be traced to a person

73
00:03:12,576 --> 00:03:13,268
and a moment,

74
00:03:13,398 --> 00:03:16,241
which is what makes the
numbers worth trusting.

75
00:03:17,871 --> 00:03:19,483
And it all fits in a pocket.

76
00:03:19,613 --> 00:03:22,096
EJO 100 installs on any
phone like an app,

77
00:03:22,226 --> 00:03:24,647
with the same data, the same
permissions,

78
00:03:24,777 --> 00:03:26,140
and the same letterhead,

79
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:28,131
wherever the work happens to
be.

80
00:03:34,171 --> 00:03:36,528
EJO 100, Enterprise
Platform.

81
00:03:36,658 --> 00:03:41,158
Built by Just Technologies
for Kewalram Chanrai Group.

82
00:03:41,288 --> 00:03:42,787
Powered by EJO 100.
